# The API key lives here and must never be committed.
.env
.env.local

# Listening verdicts recorded through the UI. These belong to whoever ran the
# demo, not to the repository, and a committed set would look like a result the
# project is asserting rather than one a reader produced.
verdicts.json

# public/state.json IS committed. It is the frozen run state a static deploy
# reads instead of /api/state, and without it a Pages deployment cannot load.

node_modules/
.DS_Store

# NOTE ON public/clips/*.wav
#
# The rendered audio IS committed, deliberately, and it is about 8 MB.
#
# An earlier version of this file ignored it, on the reasoning that the fixture
# list and the generate script are the source of truth and the wav files are
# only output. That reasoning is right for a library and wrong here. A judge
# opening the deployed site with no API key would get "not rendered" on every
# clip and no way to hear anything, which would make the deployment useless.
#
# The manifest records a sha of the text and a sha of the audio for each clip,
# and the server refuses to play any clip whose text no longer matches, so a
# committed clip cannot silently drift away from the string shown beside it.
